HST Office: closing a Writer document while a comment is being edited no longer crashes.

SwView's destructor drops its comment manager first (m_pPostItMgr.reset(); the pointer is already null while the
manager is destroyed). The manager disposes the comment windows; when the comment being edited had the keyboard focus,
vcl gives the focus back to the document window, and SwEditWin::GetFocus called HasActiveSidebarWin() on the null
manager: SIGSEGV in SwPostItMgr::HasActiveSidebarWin from SwView::~SwView (1.0.2, closing after a PDF export with
the comments in the margin, or any close with a comment in edit mode and the focus in it). GetFocus now only takes
the focus when the view has no comment manager.

